    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-payment-surcharges-act-2016-sch-1-sec-55c",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "55C Surcharge information notices",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-amendment-payment-surcharges-act-2016#sch-1-sec-55c"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-amendment-payment-surcharges-act-2016.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-amendment-payment-surcharges-act-2016.pdf, p.9",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Commission may, by written notice given to a surcharge\nparticipant, require the participant to give to the Commission\ninformation or documents evidencing either or both of the\nfollowing:\n\n(a) the amount of a payment surcharge;\n\n(b) the cost of processing a payment in relation to which a\npayment surcharge was paid.\n\n(2) A corporation is a surcharge participant if, in trade or commerce,\nthe corporation:\n\n(a) charges a payment surcharge; or\n\n(b) processes a payment for which a payment surcharge is\ncharged.\n\n(3) The notice given by the Commission to the surcharge participant is\na surcharge information notice.\n\n(4) The surcharge information notice must specify:\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2016A00009\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments\n\nCompetition and Consumer Amendment (Payment Surcharges) Act\nNo. 9, 2016\n\n(a) the kinds of information or documents to be given to the\nCommission; and\n\n(b) the period for giving the information or documents.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Commission may, by written notice given to a surcharge\nparticipant, require the participant to give to the Commission\ninformation or documents evidencing either or both of the\nfollowing:\n\n(a) the amount of a payment surcharge;\n\n(b) the cost of processing a payment in relation to which a\npayment surcharge was paid.\n\n(2) A corporation is a surcharge participant if, in trade or commerce,\nthe corporation:\n\n(a) charges a payment surcharge; or\n\n(b) processes a payment for which a payment surcharge is\ncharged.\n\n(3) The notice given by the Commission to the surcharge participant is\na surcharge information notice.\n\n(4) The surcharge information notice must specify:\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2016A00009\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments\n\nCompetition and Consumer Amendment (Payment Surcharges) Act\nNo. 9, 2016\n\n(a) the kinds of information or documents to be given to the\nCommission; and\n\n(b) the period for giving the information or documents.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-payment-surcharges-act-2016-sch-1-sec-55c-ss-1"
        },
