    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-payment-surcharges-act-2016-sch-1-sec-55e",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "55E Participant must comply with notice",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-amendment-payment-surcharges-act-2016#sch-1-sec-55e"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-amendment-payment-surcharges-act-2016.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-amendment-payment-surcharges-act-2016.pdf, p.10",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A surcharge participant commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the surcharge participant is given a surcharge information\nnotice; and\n\n(b) the surcharge participant fails to comply with the notice\nwithin the period for so complying.\nPenalty: 30 penalty units.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) is an offence of strict liability.\nNote:\nSections 137.1 and 137.2 of the Criminal Code create offences for\nproviding false or misleading information or documents.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A surcharge participant commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the surcharge participant is given a surcharge information\nnotice; and\n\n(b) the surcharge participant fails to comply with the notice\nwithin the period for so complying.\nPenalty: 30 penalty units.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) is an offence of strict liability.\nNote:\nSections 137.1 and 137.2 of the Criminal Code create offences for\nproviding false or misleading information or documents.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-payment-surcharges-act-2016-sch-1-sec-55e-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-payment-surcharges-act-2016-sch-1-sec-55e-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "2af2f04f8a01bba8bb06ebf06253d638e3ca2c40fe6529e16bacf6edc05e0468"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-amendment-payment-surcharges-act-2016#sch-1-sec-55e",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "55E Participant must comply with notice",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 10,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A surcharge participant commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the surcharge participant is given a surcharge information\nnotice; and\n\n(b) the surcharge participant fails to comply with the notice\nwithin the period for so complying.\nPenalty: 30 penalty units.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) is an offence of strict liability.\nNote:\nSections 137.1 and 137.2 of the Criminal Code create offences for\nproviding false or misleading information or documents."
    },
