      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-payment-surcharges-act-2016-sch-1-sec-55k",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "55K Effect of compliance with an infringement notice",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-amendment-payment-surcharges-act-2016#sch-1-sec-55k"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "competition-and-consumer-amendment-payment-surcharges-act-2016.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "competition-and-consumer-amendment-payment-surcharges-act-2016.pdf, p.12",
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies if:\n\n(a) an infringement notice for an alleged contravention of\nsection 55B is issued to a person; and\n\n(b) the person pays the penalty specified in the infringement\nnotice within the infringement notice compliance period and\nin accordance with the notice; and\n\n(c) the infringement notice is not withdrawn under section 55N.\n\n(2) The person is not, merely because of the payment, regarded as\nhaving contravened section 55B.\n\n(3) No proceedings (whether criminal or civil) may be started or\ncontinued against the person, by or on behalf of the\nCommonwealth, in relation to the alleged contravention of\nsection 55B.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) This section applies if:\n\n(a) an infringement notice for an alleged contravention of\nsection 55B is issued to a person; and\n\n(b) the person pays the penalty specified in the infringement\nnotice within the infringement notice compliance period and\nin accordance with the notice; and\n\n(c) the infringement notice is not withdrawn under section 55N.\n\n(2) The person is not, merely because of the payment, regarded as\nhaving contravened section 55B.\n\n(3) No proceedings (whether criminal or civil) may be started or\ncontinued against the person, by or on behalf of the\nCommonwealth, in relation to the alleged contravention of\nsection 55B.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-payment-surcharges-act-2016-sch-1-sec-55k-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-payment-surcharges-act-2016-sch-1-sec-55k-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:competition-and-consumer-amendment-payment-surcharges-act-2016-sch-1-sec-55k-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "9d2611a0f99b1b8c8b243aa984f18c463039b24a34300eda5c49ff67305c8c38"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/competition-and-consumer-amendment-payment-surcharges-act-2016#sch-1-sec-55k",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "55K Effect of compliance with an infringement notice",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 12,
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies if:\n\n(a) an infringement notice for an alleged contravention of\nsection 55B is issued to a person; and\n\n(b) the person pays the penalty specified in the infringement\nnotice within the infringement notice compliance period and\nin accordance with the notice; and\n\n(c) the infringement notice is not withdrawn under section 55N.\n\n(2) The person is not, merely because of the payment, regarded as\nhaving contravened section 55B.\n\n(3) No proceedings (whether criminal or civil) may be started or\ncontinued against the person, by or on behalf of the\nCommonwealth, in relation to the alleged contravention of\nsection 55B."
    },
